BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mimico Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T120000
UID:6ad3768ba66d123e2bd4f96c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Mimico's book for November is Crooked Cross (1934)  by Sally 
 Carson\, a recently rediscovered novel about an average German family slow
 ly succumbing to the allure of Nazism. Based on Carson's experiences livin
 g with a German family in the early 1930s\, the book is a powerful study o
 f how individuals react to personal\, political and cultural pressure.\nCo
 pies available at the library.\nCrooked Cross
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad3768ba66d123e2bd4f96c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
