BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto's Ravines: Nature and History at Your Doorstep
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T150000
UID:6a67676ecca66c2f00a645ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's ravine landscapes are not just a sanctuary for wildl
 ife\; they also protect the city against flooding and allow us to enjoy na
 ture at our doorsteps. This presentation by the Toronto Field Naturalists 
 shares how the ravines are changing over time\; how they are responding to
  numerous pressures and how you can explore and help protect them.\nPresen
 ter Bio:\nEllen Schwartzel is a former president of the Toronto Field Natu
 ralists\, and she enjoys leading walks through Toronto's ravines.  Ellen's
  career in environmental policy included 23 years with the Environmental C
 ommissioner of Ontario. She was Ontario's Deputy Environmental Commissione
 r for four years\, until retiring in 2018.  Ellen’s academic training wa
 s in Botany\, and she received her BSc and MSc at the University of Toront
 o.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, su
 pported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a67676ecca66c2f00a645ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T150000
UID:6ad76edbfee2d21deb2483fb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWhat    
   you need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe      risk of fr
 acturing a bone\nHow      to maintain healthy bones\nImpact      of nutrit
 ion & physical activity Fall prevention\nPresentations are delivered by tr
 ained volunteers on behalf of Osteoporosis Canada.\n*Registration required
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad76edbfee2d21deb2483fb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
