BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Make a Will with Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T153000
UID:6ade51a4901b02002cc50ea3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month\, and TPL is delighted to host t
 he Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will an
 d powers of attorney for you and your family. Carissa DeMarinis\, a membe
 r of the\nOntario Bar Association\nwho practices Will\, Trusts and Estates
  Law will speak about the elements of a will\, what happens if you don’t
  have one\, what are powers of attorney\, why they are important\, and spe
 cial considerations to keep in mind when preparing your estate and care pl
 ans. Please note that this program is for general information only\, not 
 for drafting individual wills.\nRegistration required\n. Registrants need 
 to check in with staff by\n2:05 pm\nto hold their spot. Drop-ins are wel
 come until capacity is reached.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ade51a4901b02002cc50ea3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
