BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) for Healthy Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T163000
UID:6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d59@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being
 —whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or s
 imply wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRA
 P for Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is e
 xpertly designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the 
 principles of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging 
 challenges.\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experie
 nce with WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skill
 s.\nParticipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program 
 completion\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. F
 ind more WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every S
 unday\, once a week for 3 weeks November 8 - November 22. Week 1 will be 
 3 hours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  WRAP\; Weeks 2 and
  3 will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided\n.\nSnacks and 
 refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nHope 
 + Me\n. Hope + Me is solely responsible for the protection of personal inf
 ormation collected through the program registration process.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac902fa295b3b0033cb0d59
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
