BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ACT-ively Preventing Elder Abuse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T160000
UID:6aaea5c3f5c6780c7049389e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to reco
 gnize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of 
 the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to:\n
 · identify the different types of elder abuse\n· Identify the signs of e
 lder abuse\n· Using theatre exercises\, develop strategies to be an 'acti
 ve bystander' in situations where elder abuse might be present. No theatre
  experience required\, but participation in role plays is encouraged!\nAbo
 ut Theatre of the Beat:\nTheatre of the Beat (TOTB) is a Canadian touring 
 theatre company working to catalyze conversations on social justice and it
 s intersection with the beliefs of the communities in which we find oursel
 ves.\nLight refreshments are provided for all participants.\nRegistration 
 is encouraged.  Please register online.\nInformation Collection Notice: T
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
