BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors Club - Birds in Winter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T150000
UID:6a6cb34888e9bf28003497f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Cliffcrest invites all to our Seniors Club! Hang out and enjoy
  games\, engaging presentations and workshops on a variety of topics.\nThi
 s Month: Birds in Winter\nWinter is a harsh season\, yet many birds stay i
 n Toronto and survive. Why don’t they all fly south? How do they stay wa
 rm and find food and shelter? Which birds stay and which ones migrate? Lea
 rn about migrant birds and their incredible journeys\, visiting birds who 
 come to the city from their boreal and Arctic homes\, and our resident bir
 ds who spend the long\, cold winter months here.\nJoin Monika Croydon\, av
 id local birder and member of the Toronto Ornithological Club\, to find ou
 t how we can all help birds in winter\, from providing feeders and creatin
 g bird-friendly gardens and homes\, to supporting conservation and researc
 h as Citizen Scientists.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6cb34888e9bf28003497f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
