BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto's Ravines
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T170000
UID:6ab565f6ca248a0029182aae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's ravine landscapes are not just a sanctuary for wildl
 ife\; they also protect the city against flooding and allow us to enjoy na
 ture at our doorsteps. This presentation by the Toronto Field Naturalists 
 shares how the ravines are changing over time\; how they are responding to
  numerous pressures and how you can explore and help protect them.\nPresen
 ter Bio:\nEllen Schwartzel is a former president of the Toronto Field Natu
 ralists\, and she enjoys leading walks through Toronto's ravines.  Ellen's
  career in environmental policy included 23 years with the Environmental C
 ommissioner of Ontario. She was Ontario's Deputy Environmental Commissione
 r for four years\, until retiring in 2018.  Ellen’s academic training wa
 s in Botany\, and she received her BSc and MSc at the University of Toront
 o.\nDrop In\, No Registration is Required.\nPlease contact Long Branch\, 4
 16-394-5320 with any inquiries.
LOCATION:Long Branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab565f6ca248a0029182aae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
