BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Launch: Lisa Hanawalt's I Can't Stop Thinking About Horses an
 d Sex
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6acfc848a76c9f3e2ae8291f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join\nLisa Hanawalt\nin conversation with\nAnn Fitzpatrick\nas
  she launches\nI Can’t Stop Thinking About Horses and Sex.\nI Can’t St
 op Thinking About Horses and Sex\nmarks Hanawalt’s long-awaited return t
 o comics. In this brutally honest\, vulnerable yet still irreverently funn
 y memoir\, a horse girl now in her forties  reflects back on a lifetime of
  obsessions and confronts the many hurdles of a life fully lived.\nFrom co
 nfronting whether or not to have kids\, to being an anxious lil’ freak\,
  to caring for a sick horse\, to dealing with a major breakup and the ensu
 ing lustfulness—Hanawalt delivers a reading experience that’s relatabl
 e\, affirming\, and absolutely hilarious.\nLisa Hanawalt\nis an artist and
  writer living in Los Angeles\, CA. She is the creator of the animated ser
 ies\nTuca & Bertie\nand the production designer/producer on\nBoJack Horsem
 an\nand\nLong Story Short\n. Lisa has published four books with Drawn & Qu
 arterly: M\ny Dirty Dumb Eyes\, Hot Dog Taste Test\, Coyote Doggirl\,\nand
 \nI Want You\n. Her fifth book\,\nI Can't Stop Thinking About Horses and S
 ex\nhas already garnered rave reviews from\nNPR\, LitHub\, Vulture\nand\nP
 ublishers Weekly.\nAnna Fitzpatrick\nis the author of the novel\nGood Girl
 \n(Flying Books) and the picture book\nMargot and the Moon Landing\n(Annic
 k Press). She was a full-time writer until Toronto rent prices forced her 
 to get a day job\, and now she works at a nonprofit that advocates for aff
 ordable housing.\nAdvance praise for\nI Can’t Stop Thinking About Horses
  and Sex\n“Lisa Hanawalt draws and writes the things we all wish we coul
 d say: about love\, loss\, and what it feels like to be in a human body."
 —Lena Dunham\n"I can't stop thinking about how this is the best and funn
 iest and most vulnerable book about being a horny girl who loves both hors
 es and Kevin Costner that I have ever read."—Samantha Irby\n“I couldn
 ’t put this book down! I read it in one night which felt like a sleepove
 r with a tender\, bold\, hilarious friend who knew everything about me\; n
 othing was shameful when we were together.”—Miranda July\n"Ironies of 
 life: Here she’s all obsessed with horses and riding horses\, and she ha
 s this big ass\, which she openly admits to and draws...and here I am obse
 ssed with women with big asses and wanting to jump on them and ride them l
 ike horses. I guess I should write back to Lisa and ask her if she’d giv
 e me a ride on her big ass. She’d probably say no. Ironies of life."—R
 . Crumb.\nBooks will be available for purchase with the Beguiling book sto
 re.\nI Want You\nCoyote Doggirl\nGood Girl
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6acfc848a76c9f3e2ae8291f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
