DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6a84c31960ccaf01c01f27a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy Gardening? Novice or expert\, join us on the thir
 d Tuesday of the month at 7 pm for an hour of Gardening talks.\nOct 20\nPl
 anting Bulbs in the Fall for Spring Glory\nPlanting bulbs in the fall will
  bring glorious rewards in your spring garden. A Toronto Master Gardener w
 ill give advice on what to plant\, how to plant them and yes\, even a few 
 pointers on squirrels! At the end of the program\, bulbs will be given out
  to attendees\, while supplies last.\nSuitable for gardeners of any skill 
 level\, with any kind of outdoor space.\nNov 17\nOrchid: Daunting Diva\, E
 vocative Evolutionary or Humble Houseplant?\nThe Orchid is now the world
 ’s MOST popular houseplant. Facilitated by a Toronto Master Gardener\, l
 earn fascinating stories\, fun facts and tips on orchid care. Love them al
 ready but yours don’t bloom? Don’t fret! We have answers. Have disease
  and pest problems? We help you solve them. Plus\, the best orchids to gro
 w in your home. Suitable for gardeners of any skill level.\nDec  15       
  TBC
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84c31960ccaf01c01f27a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
