UID:6ad24ff5ebad22004545d31e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a 6-week course designed to build y
 our confidence by introducing new skills slowly in a small\, supportive co
 mmunity. At the end of the course\, you may not know everything about the 
 internet\, but you will have a solid foundation of new skills and the conf
 idence to continue learning.\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as th
 e mouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services 
 and entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and frien
 ds\nInternet safety\, security and privacy\nWeek 1:\nUse the Mouse\nWeek 2
 :\nUse the Keyboard\nWeek 3:\nUse Windows\nWeek 4:\nUse the Internet\nWeek
  5:\nUse Google Search & Maps\nWeek 6:\nUse Email (Gmail)\nThe class is li
 mited to\n8\nparticipants. Registration is required\, please register on t
 he TPL website. If you need any assistance with registering\, please visit
  us in-branch\, or call us at 416-393-7674. When registering\, you will be
  registered for the entire series.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad24ff5ebad22004545d31e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
