UID:6aec9547ad40276591564539@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being—wh
 ether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simply
  wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRAP for W
 ellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is expertly
  designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the princip
 les of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging challen
 ges\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experience with
  WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skills.\nPart
 icipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program completi
 on\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. Find more
  WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every\nThursday
 \, once a week for 3 weeks\, November 5 - November 19.\nWeek 1 will be 3 h
 ours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  WRAP\; Weeks 2 and 3
  will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided\n.\nSnacks and re
 freshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nHope + Me\n
 . Hope + Me is solely responsible for the protection of personal informati
 on collected through the program registration process.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aec9547ad40276591564539
