BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Benefits and Credits for Adults 65 Years & Older
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T150000
UID:6ae23f06901b02002cc5c3e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This presentation by the Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) provides 
 an overview of the income sources\, benefits\, credits\, and tax measures 
 available to seniors. It explains retirement income programs such as Old A
 ge Security (OAS)\, the Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\, and private pensions\,
  and highlights the importance of filing a tax return every year to receiv
 e benefit payments and maintain eligibility for programs.\nThe presentatio
 n also covers key tax credits and deductions available to seniors\, includ
 ing the Age Amount\, Pension Income Amount\, Medical Expense Tax Credit\, 
 Home Accessibility Tax Credit\, Disability Tax Credit\, and pension income
  splitting. In addition\, it shares information on free tax-filing assista
 nce.\nDrop in.  No registration required.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae23f06901b02002cc5c3e5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
