UID:6ad3a492a76c9f3e2ae87b5e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Estate Planning and Wills\nNovember is Financial Literacy Mont
 h!\nPlanning for the future is an important step in protecting your wishes
  and providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\nJoin us for an 
 informative session with guest lawyer\nSarita Samaroo\, principal lawyer o
 f SST Law Professional Corporation\n\, as she discusses the importance of 
 estate planning.and wills.\nLearn about the key elements of a will\, what 
 happens if you don't have one\, Powers of Attorney\, and important conside
 rations when planning your estate. Discover helpful information and resour
 ces to better understand your options and take the next steps in planning 
 for the future.\nThis program is presented in partnership with Financial E
 mpowerment Services at Malvern Library and North York Community House.\nFo
 llowing the presentation\, there will be an opportunity to ask questions a
 nd connect with Financial Empowerment staff for additional support.\nRegis
 ter online. Drop-ins welcome.\nThis session is for general information pur
 poses only and does not include the preparation of individual wills or per
 sonalized legal advice.
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad3a492a76c9f3e2ae87b5e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
