UID:6ac6de6d96ec3a003ad9124e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this workshop\
 , participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-step in
 structions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own g
 eometric pattern and complex design art pieces.\nInformation Collection No
