BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How Pleasant to Know Mr. Lear
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T150000
UID:6a751cd8f213992f00ca3065@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dennis Duffy\, Professor Emeritus\, Department of English\, U
 niversity of Toronto\, discusses the genius of Edward Lear as a painter a
 nd poet\, the great joiner of oil painting and printed nonsense.\nLear was
  a singular eccentric in his bespoke but loosely-fitting suits and his run
 cible hat\, he created work placing him among the finest of graphic cartoo
 nists and satirists. This presentation explores that jagged world that he 
 made up for himself\, in order to preserve his own complex selfhood.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a751cd8f213992f00ca3065
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
