BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Low Income Retirement Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085de@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month\nLearn about government b
 enefits\, tax credits\, and strategies to help protect your retirement inc
 ome. Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario.\nThese sessions
  are designed for seniors with low income and those who advise them.\nRegi
 stration not required. Drop-in welcome.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Seniors 
 Get?\nLearn about benefits for older adults living in Ontario\, including 
 Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\, Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income Sup
 plement (GIS)\, and Guaranteed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursday
  Oct 15: Understanding the Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxable 
 income and how can tax credits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemptions 
 help to reduce taxable income.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retiremen
 t Income.\nLearn how to reduce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if re
 ceiving additional income from employment\, a private pension\, or a Regis
 tered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada a
 nd Leaving Canada.\nLearn about eligible benefits for those that resided 
 in Canada for fewer than 40 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for t
 hose planning on emigrating from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26: 
 Tax Credits and Benefits for Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLearn 
 about other tax credits and benefits for seniors\, people with disabilitie
 s\, and caregivers\, including the disability tax credit\, the Canada care
 giver credit\, and the home accessibility tax credit.\nOne-on-one support 
 is available at select branches. Meet with Financial Empowerment staff for
  free financial counselling. Book your free appointment today. Speak with 
 branch staff or visit\ntpl.ca/financial-empowerment\nfor more information.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085de
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
