BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alderwood Book Club: Clara at the Door With a Revolver
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6adb9ff20b801373af90d0ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In November we will be discussing the non-fiction book\nClara 
 at the Door With a Revolver\nby Carolyn Whitzman.\n“In the autumnal dark
 ness of October 6\, 1894\, an unseen figure rang the doorbell at the Parkd
 ale home of a well-to-do Toronto family and then shot eighteen-year-old Fr
 ank Westwood in his doorway\, murdering him in cold blood.\nSix weeks late
 r\, Clara Ford\, a Black tailor and single mother\, was arrested. Known fo
 r her impeccable work ethic and her resolute personality - and for her pre
 dilection for wearing men’s attire – she confessed to the murder.\nBut
  as the details of her arrest and her complex connection to the Westwood f
 amily emerged\, Clara recanted\, testifying that she had been coerced by p
 olice into a false confession.”\nCopies of the book are available at Ald
 erwood Branch in regular print. Ebook versions available from tpl.ca
LOCATION:Alderwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adb9ff20b801373af90d0ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
