BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) for Healthy Aging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T160000
UID:6abc1b8fe8cf1c005cafeaae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for anyone looking to strengthen their well-being
 —whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or s
 imply wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. The WRA
 P for Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Workshop for Healthy Aging is e
 xpertly designed by Hope + Me for individuals aged 60 and older using the 
 principles of WRAP\, but with scenarios and tools focused on common aging 
 challenges\nThis 3-week session is appropriate for people with no experien
 ce with WRAP\, or for those who wish to refresh their knowledge and skills
 .\nParticipants will receive a certificate of participation upon program c
 ompletion\, but these sessions do not contribute to a WRAP certificate. Fi
 nd more WRAP program options at TPL\nhere.\nThis WRAP Group meets every Fr
 iday\, once a week for 3 weeks\, November 13\, November 20\, November 27.)
  Week 1 will be 3 hours\, with a 30 minute overview and orientation of  W
 RAP\; Weeks 2 and 3 will be 2.5 hours.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provide
 d\n.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredien
 t lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaborat
 ion with\nHope + Me\n. Hope + Me is solely responsible for the protection 
 of personal information collected through the program registration process
 .
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc1b8fe8cf1c005cafeaae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
