DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T200000
UID:6ae36574ebad22004548d0c1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program provides an overview of the six key record groups
  for effective genealogical research\, including the information you can e
 xpect to find in the records\, and where you'll find them. Participants wi
 ll come away from this program with an enhanced understanding of the major
  sources of information that are available for learning about their ancest
 ors who lived in Ontario before 1867.\nJanice Nickerson is a professional 
 genealogist who specializes in Upper Canadian history. She is also the aut
 hor of\nCrime and Punishment in Upper Canada.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
