BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Human Connection 101 Workshop for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T193000
UID:6ae394ac377296003a4f8d32@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive workshop to learn practical ways to enhance social health\,
  understand the adverse effects of loneliness\, and discover the benefits 
 of building more meaningful connections. Receive a free social health work
 book\, spend time with other participants after the workshops\, and enjoy 
 some light refreshments provided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 2016\, GenWel
 l is a registered charity whose mission is to make the world a happier and
  healthier place by educating\, empowering\, and catalyzing forty million 
 Canadians about the importance of their social health.\nRegistration for t
 his program is required\, however\, drop-ins will be accepted\n5 minutes\n
 after the program starts.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal in
 formation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under th
 e Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informati
 on will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eva
 luation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be d
 irected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Y
 onge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae394ac377296003a4f8d32
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
