SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Broken Land
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T150000
UID:6adb6fa9fee2d21deb253dea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of  Broken Land movie.\nCarson Tidwell wants nothing more than to be lef
 t alone on his rural Texas ranch. When he accidentally shoots a pregnant m
 igrant worker crossing his land\, he feels compelled to protect her from h
 is estranged Border Patrol agent son. As she recovers\, a bond forms that 
 ultimately heals them both.\nRated PG13. 1hr 40 mins.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adb6fa9fee2d21deb253dea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
