BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ACT-ively Preventing Elder Abuse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T160000
UID:6ad1507a9d27a00045513767@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to reco
 gnize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of 
 the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to:\n
 identify the different types of elder abuse\nIdentify the signs of elder a
 buse\nUsing theatre exercises\, develop strategies to be an 'active bystan
 der' in situations where elder abuse might be present. No theatre experien
 ce required\, but participation in role plays is encouraged!\nLight refres
 hments\nare provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availa
 ble at the program.\nThis is a\ndrop-in\nprogram for up to 30 people. No r
 egistration is required.\nAbout Theatre of the Beat:\nTheatre of the Beat 
 (TOTB) is a Canadian touring theatre company working to catalyze conversat
 ions on social justice and its intersection with the beliefs of the commun
 ities in which we find ourselves.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad1507a9d27a00045513767
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
