BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memory and Aging: What's Normal\, What's Not\, and What You Can Do
  About It
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T120000
UID:6aee44689d27a000455635ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Psychologist Dr. Nicole Anderson discusses kinds of cogniti
 ve functions change as a part of healthy aging\, and provides examples of 
 normal memory slips\, and not so normal memory slips. This presentation di
 scusses factors affecting cognition\, including medical factors\, and ever
 yday lifestyle factors\, then provides a number of memory strategies that 
 people can use to make their memory function better.\nDr. Anderson is the 
 Senior Scientist at the Rotman Research Institute (Baycrest) and  Professo
 r\, Psychology and Psychiatry (University of Toronto). She is the author o
 f\nLiving With Mild Cognitive Impairment\n.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aee44689d27a000455635ae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
