BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T160000
UID:6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Staying connected with family\, keeping track of appointments\
 , finding programs that interest you. AI can help with everyday things. No
  jargon\, no pressure\, no experience needed.\nIn this class with our Inno
 vator-in-Residence\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll learn how AI can help you writ
 e a message in your own voice\, turn a spoken thought into a checklist\, p
 lan questions for an appointment\, and find community programs. We'll also
  talk straight about the risks: AI that sounds like a person deserves caut
 ion\, and we'll practice spotting the scams that use it. You'll leave with
  large-print materials\, one personally useful template\, and a simple fam
 ily safety phrase\, all at your own pace.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboar
 ding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding experience r
 equired.\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\, 2026 at 12:
 30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the star
 t of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a f
 irst come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to s
 ave your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own USB stick
 .\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes activiti
 es that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do no
 t need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants are enco
 uraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which inc
 lude best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy s
 tatements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLear
 n more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more ab
 out the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about th
 e tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
