BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afternoon Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T143000
UID:6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7948@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books i
 n a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th\, October 19th\, Novemb
 er 9th\, and December 14th.\nThis month we will be reading\nThe MANIAC\nby
  Benjamin Labatut.\nThe MANIAC\nis a 2023 novel by Chilean author Benjami
 n Labatut\, and his first in English (compared to his usual Spanish). It 
 is a fictionalized biography of polymath John von Neumann interwoven with 
 tripartite narratives exploring the intersection of human genius\, ration
 ality\, and artificial intelligence.Told via oral-history style from peers
 \, wives\, and colleagues\, Labatut attempts to decipher core themes of re
 ason and madness\, the edge of progress\, and the loss of the sacred. Whi
 le a spiritual sequel to\nWhen We Cease to Understand the World\n\,\nno pr
 ior knowledge of science or technology is needed to appreciate Labatut's p
 olymathic portrait of von Neumann.\nParticipants can borrow a copy of the 
 book from the Woodside Square branch upon registration.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7948
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
