DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nSnowbound: Animals in winter\nHow do animals l
 ive in extreme cold where temperatures can reach −50°C or lower? Throug
 h a combination of physical adaptations\, behavioral strategies\, speciali
 zed senses and remarkable biological processes they are able to thrive. In
  fact\, reindeer\, for example\, really do have red noses because they are
  packed with extra blood vessels that help them regulate their body temper
 ature and keeps their brains warm. Closed Captions. 60 minutes. 2017.
