BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Birth of Modern Forensics – 1910-1940
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261228T190000
UID:6af4df4b08e64c003ab88f5b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​The Birth of Modern Forensics explores the science of early
 -twentieth-century forensics\, how it changed and expanded. It explores th
 e social context in which these changes occurred. Not every law enforcemen
 t agent welcomed the presence of interlopers\, of the fame they received f
 or “solving” a crime. The success and perseverance on the part of the 
 first forensic scientists ushered in a new era and changed criminal invest
 igations forever.\nThis program is being presented by Kerry Cathers\, who
  runs the research resource websites\nA Curiosity of Crime\nand\nBandit
 ’s Roost\nfor authors of historical detective fiction (1800-1940)\nRegi
 stration is encouraged\, and we welcome drop-in customers until capacity i
 s reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af4df4b08e64c003ab88f5b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
