BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Afternoon Movie - The Best Christmas Pageant Ever (2025)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T160000
UID:6aa8076886d845003115ef39@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Herdmans are absolutely the worst kids in the history of t
 he world. They lie\, they steal\, they bully...and now they've hijacked th
 e town Christmas pageant. Directed by Dallas Jenkins and based on the inte
 rnational best seller by Barbara Robinson. Six siblings who sneak into chu
 rch searching for snacks and walk away with the lead roles in the town pag
 eant. Grace (Judy Greer) is directing the performance for the very first 
 time\; she and her daughter Beth (Molly Belle Wright) and husband Bob (Pet
 e Holmes) are in over their heads\, especially against a town that wants t
 hem to kick the Herdmans out. But the play's mischievous stars might unwit
 tingly teach a community the true meaning of Christmas.\nPG\, 99 minutes\n
 **Subtitles for the deaf and hard of hearing when available (SDH).
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa8076886d845003115ef39
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
