SUMMARY:AI and Creativity: Can Technology Inspire the Human Imagination?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270112T190000
UID:6ad8f041e9f71840dd72aea6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This presentation explores the increasingly complicated relati
 onship between technology and creativity. Rather than treating AI as simpl
 y good or bad\, participants consider whether technology can generate crea
 tive sparks while examining the distinctly human elements of imagination\,
  subjective experience\, choice and authorship. Drawing on more than 30 ye
 ars in magazines\, writing and publishing presented by international award
  winning author Lisa de Nikolits.\nRegistration required.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
