UID:69c980df81b67dfe32afc3a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us to share the joy of reading\, while building climate r
 esilience knowledge. Members are invited to discuss a book they are readin
 g\, tell stories\,  and empower each other to explore community-driven sol
 utions. Each party will start with a quiet read and reflect time\, with op
 portunities to join group discussions later on over refreshments.\nAUGUST\
 n– Fossil Fuel Folly\nAmerican War\nby Omar El Akkad or your favourite d
 ystopian read!\nor your favourite book featuring water!\nSEPTEMBER\n– We
  Need Pollinators\nThe History of Bees\nby Maja Lunde or your favourite an
 imal-centred book!\nOCTOBER\n– Climate Change is Scary\nThe Annual Migra
 tion of Clouds\nby Premee Mohamed or a different book that shares a scary 
 future ecological crisis!\nNOVEMBER\n- Climate Changes Everything\nMinistr
 y for the Future\nby Kim Stanley Robinson or your favourite time travel re
 ad!\nCopies are available in the branch to pick up\, while supplies last.\
 nRegistration is encouraged but drop ins are welcome!\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
