BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270130T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270130T150000
UID:6aef8b9c377296003a51cde3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program will address the experiences of families who are 
 caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, including the various
  points of stress\, as well as the various points of joy\, and ways in whi
 ch caregivers learn to survive the experience. Major topics include unders
 tanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, choosing an ass
 isted living facility\, and using music and the arts as a means of connect
 ion.\nPresented by D. Grant Campbell\, author of "Surviving Dementia Care:
  The Realities of Caregiving" (University of Toronto Press\, 2026).\nPleas
 e note the author will be available after the event to sign copies of his 
 book.\nPlease register online.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
