BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History of True Crime Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270211T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270211T160000
UID:6af22da0ebad2200454b81d5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the\nHistory of True Crime\nBook Club where we\nd
 iscuss crimes of the past by way of great non-fiction books.\nJoin us mont
 hly for a lively discussion of our selected titles\nwhere we will explore
  topics such as violence\, corruption\, ideology\, and so much more.\nJan
  14 -\nSay Nothing\nby Patrick Radden Keefe\nFeb 11 -\nAmerican Heiress\nb
 y Jeffrey Toobin\nMar 11 -\nKillers of the Flower Moon\nby David Grann\nAp
 r 8 –\nThe Central Park Five\nby Sarah Burns\nMay 13 –\nThe Whisky Kin
 g\nby Trevor Cole\nJun 10 –\nHomegrown\nby Jeffrey Toobin\nJul 8 –\nTh
 e Massey Murder\nby Charlotte Gray\nAug 12 –\nThe Big Short\nby Michael 
 Lewis\nSept 9 –\nEmpire of Pain\nby Patrick Radden Keefe\nOct 14 –\nSh
 ackled\nby Candy Cooper\nNov 11 –\nBad Blood\nby John Carreyrou\nDec 9 
 –\nThat Lonely Section of Hell\nby Lorimer Shenher\nJan 13\, 2028 –\nS
 even Fallen Feathers\nby Tanya Talaga\nFeb 10\, 2028 –\nThe Fort Bragg C
 artel\nby Seth Harp\nMar 9\, 2028 –\nAdnan's Story\nby Rabia Chaudry\nBo
 oks will be distributed at each meeting (While supplies last).\nA Library 
 card will be required to check them out.\n(These titles are subject to cha
 nge)\nRegistration Required.\nRegister online\, by phone or in person\nat 
 Humanities & Social Science Desk\, 416-393-7175
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founders' Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af22da0ebad2200454b81d5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
