BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to Grow Native Plants From Seed: Sowing In a Winter Wonderla
 nd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270213T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270213T150000
UID:6ae8cceb5ea4c386b3ec4abe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Who says you can’t grow a garden in the winter? Winter sowin
 g is an easy and inexpensive way to start native seeds. Through this simpl
 e method of sowing seeds during the colder months\, you can plan your gard
 en to support butterflies\, bees and birds.\nIn this workshop\, learn how 
 surprisingly easy it is to grow native wildflowers from seed if we follow 
 nature’s lead by embracing the cold!\nIn this presentation\, Dorte Windm
 uller\, a Butterflyway Ranger of the David Suzuki Foundation\, will lead a
  hands-on experience of seed cleaning and packing. Participants can take 
 some seed packets home for your garden or balcony.\nThis program is part o
 f TPL's\nOur Fragile\nPlanet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Tor
 onto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae8cceb5ea4c386b3ec4abe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
